# p_8e2f — Marco's full work kit: lunchbox and vitamins leave, journal stays (fork of p_b7c2)

This fork of p_b7c2 refines which items Marco actually carries to his afternoon-to-night shift. The parent document claimed all three—lunchbox, vitamins, and journal—leave at 13:40. The evidence so far supports the lunchbox going out strongly (10 empty looks at cupboard_k1 vs 1 in-house sighting) and the vitamins going out moderately (5 empty looks at counter_k1 vs 1 in-house sighting). However, the journal has only 3 weak-for looks at nightstand_b1 vs 1 against, and Marco's stated hobby is "journaling" in the evening (22:30–00:00), which suggests he needs it at home. A more parsimonious reading: Marco packs his lunchbox and takes his vitamins (a small pill organizer he clips to his bag), but leaves the journal on the nightstand because he journals before bed.

What changed from the parent: journal_marco no longer goes OUT_OF_HOUSE. It stays at nightstand_b1 throughout the work shift. The lunchbox and vitamins blocks are retained. A new claim tests whether the journal is still at the nightstand at 16:00 on a weekday (when Marco is at work).

What would refute this fork: the journal sighted OUT_OF_HOUSE or at desk_b1 during 14:00–22:00 on a weekday (it should be at nightstand_b1); the lunchbox at cupboard_k1 during 14:00–22:00 (it should be out).

